+# Command Surface Unification — Design
+
+**Date:** 2026-07-16
+**Status:** Proposal (design only — no renames implemented)
+**Owner ask:** Extend the `forge memory` unification pattern across the whole CLI.
+Cluster related operations under a small set of intuitive BASE commands (nouns)
+with clear SUBCOMMANDS — like `gh pr create`, `git remote add`, `docker container ls`
+— so the surface is *learnable*, not a flat sprawl of ~40+ top-level verbs.
+"Making a unique base command for each doesn't make sense; we need a simple
+surface and subcommands to map things properly."
+
+---
+
+## 1. Current surface audit
+
+`node bin/forge.js --help` + the command files under `lib/commands/*.js` yield
+**57 registered top-level command files**. Registration is auto-discovery:
+`lib/commands/_registry.js` scans the dir, validates `{ name, description, handler }`,
+and a static `_manifest.js` provides the bundleable fast path.
+
+### Already grouped (noun + subcommand)
+| Base | Subcommands |
+|------|-------------|
+| `issue` | create, update, claim, release, comment, close, show, list, ready, search, stats, blocked, stale, orphans, lint, children, owns, claims, dep |
+| `worktree` | create, remove, list |
+| `gate` | enable, disable, approve, reject, status, check |
+| `release` | `<id>` (release claim) \| `check` (readiness) |
+| `patch` | record, status |
+| `adapter` | test, list, enable, disable |
+| `new` | `<kind> <name>` (scaffold) |
+| `team` | (coordination utilities) |
+
+### Flat top-level verbs (the sprawl)
+`adapter, add, audit, blocked, board, claim, claims, clean, close, comment,
+create, dev, doc-gate, doctor, explain, export, gate, hooks, init, insights,
+issue, issues, lint, list, merge, migrate, new, options, orient, orphans,
+patch, plan, preflight, prime, push, ready, recall, recap, recommend, release,
+remember, role, setup, shepherd, ship, show, stage, stale, status, sync, team,
+test, update, upgrade, validate, worktree`
+
+### The existing precedent (this is the model to generalise)
+`bin/forge.js:2318` defines `ISSUE_ALIAS_COMMANDS` — a curated allowlist of bare
+verbs (`create, update, claim, close, show, list, ready, blocked, stale,
+orphans, lint, claims, issues`) that stay **registered + routable for
+back-compat** but are **hidden from `forge --help`** so `forge issue` reads as
+the single canonical surface (kernel issue `450c6e34`). `parseFlags()` skips
+global flag parsing for these so flags pass through to the issue handler intact.
+
+**This is exactly the pattern to extend:** canonical noun group is the documented
+form; a curated set of hot verbs *also* exist as top-level aliases; help shows the
+noun, not the sprawl.
+
+### The `memory` reference pattern — reality check
+There is **no `memory.js` command today**. `forge memory --help` falls through to
+the generic help. `remember` and `recall` are two separate top-level files
+(`remember.js`/`recall.js`) writing/reading the same kernel-backed store. So the
+"memory unification" is *aspirational* — this design defines it and makes it the
+template: introduce a `memory` base that owns `save`(remember)/`recall`/`insights`,
+with `remember`/`recall` kept as top-level ergonomic aliases.
+
+---
+
+## 2. External CLI patterns (grounding the taxonomy)
+
+- **`gh` (GitHub CLI)** — strict `gh <noun> <verb>`: `gh pr create`, `gh issue list`,
+  `gh repo clone`. Nouns are the primary organising axis; near-zero bare verbs.
+  User-defined `gh alias set` covers personal ergonomics. *(cli.github.com/manual)*
+- **`git`** — hybrid: hottest porcelain verbs are top-level (`git status`,
+  `git commit`, `git push`, `git log`) while multi-op areas are noun-grouped
+  (`git remote add`, `git stash push`, `git worktree add`, `git submodule update`).
+  Proves a *curated* top-level verb set can coexist with noun groups.
+- **`docker`** — migrated from flat verbs (`docker run`, `docker rm`, `docker pull`)
+  to **management commands** (`docker container run`, `docker image pull`). Legacy
+  top-level verbs are retained for back-compat and can be hidden via
+  `DOCKER_HIDE_LEGACY_COMMANDS`, leaving only the noun groups. *(docs.docker.com/reference/cli/docker)*
+  — This is the closest precedent to Forge's situation and to the existing
+  `ISSUE_ALIAS_COMMANDS` mechanism.
+- **`cargo`** — flat verbs (`cargo build/test/run/publish`) because the surface is
+  small and single-domain. Lesson: don't nest when a domain is small and flat.
+- **`kubectl`** — `<verb> <noun>` (`kubectl get pods`) — inverse axis, works because
+  verbs are a tiny fixed set (get/apply/delete/describe). Forge's verbs are open-ended,
+  so **noun-first (gh/docker model) fits better**.
+
+**Design takeaways:** (1) noun-first grouping for learnability; (2) a *curated
+allowlist* of hot verbs stays top-level (git/docker precedent) — never nest the
+daily hot path; (3) don't over-nest small single-domain areas; (4) grouping is a
+help/organisation concern layered over a flat routable registry — back-compat is free.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Proposed taxonomy — 8 base nouns + `team`, over a curated hot-verb layer
+
+Two tiers, exactly like git/docker:
+
+- **Tier A — top-level ergonomic verbs** (always work, *never gain keystrokes*):
+  workflow stages + the daily hot path. Each is *also* reachable via its canonical
+  noun where one exists (a documented alias, like `git status` ≡ nothing-nested but
+  `docker pull` ≡ `docker image pull`).
+- **Tier B — canonical noun groups** (the learnable, documented surface). `--help`
+  shows Tier B; Tier A hot verbs get a short "shortcuts" footer; the rest of the
+  bare aliases are hidden (extends `ISSUE_ALIAS_COMMANDS`).
+
+### Base nouns
+
+| Base | Owns (canonical subcommands) | Rationale |
+|------|------------------------------|-----------|
+| `issue` *(exists)* | create, update, claim, release, comment, close, show, list, ready, search, stats, blocked, stale, orphans, lint, children, owns, claims, dep, **stage**, **recap**, **export**, **sync** | Work-item lifecycle + per-issue reads. Fold in `comment/stage/recap` (per-issue) and `export/sync` (operate on the issue store). |
+| `memory` *(new)* | **save** (=remember), **recall**, **insights** | Knowledge persistence. The reference pattern, realised. |
+| `worktree` *(exists)* | create, remove, list, **clean** | Isolated workspaces. `clean` (remove merged worktrees + ff default) belongs here. |
+| `gate` *(exists)* | enable, disable, approve, reject, status, check, **doc** (=doc-gate) | Workflow gates + approvals. `doc-gate` is literally a gate → `gate doc`. |
+| `pr` *(new)* | **ship** (create PR), **preflight**, **shepherd**, **merge** | Everything that acts on a pull request. |
+| `config` *(new)* | **init**, **setup**, **options**, **role**, **recommend**, **explain**, **hooks** | Configure the project + runtime + adoption profile. |
+| `ext` *(new)* | **new**, **add**, **adapter**, **audit**, **patch** | Extend Forge: scaffolds, lockfile sources, review adapters, audit, patch intent. |
+| `env` *(new)* | **doctor**, **upgrade**, **migrate** | Runtime health, lifecycle, migration. |
+| `team` *(exists)* | coordination, **board** (team runtime board) | Multi-agent coordination. `board` is a team view. |
+
+### Full per-verb mapping
+
+| Current verb | Canonical form | Top-level alias kept? | Tier |
+|--------------|----------------|-----------------------|------|
+| plan | `plan` (stage) | canonical top-level | A (stage) |
+| dev | `dev` (stage) | canonical top-level | A (stage) |
+| validate | `validate` (stage) | canonical top-level | A (stage) |
+| ship | `pr ship` | **yes** (`ship`) | A (stage) |
+| review / verify | (skills, no command file) | canonical top-level | A (stage) |
+| status | `status` | canonical top-level | A (hot) |
+| test | `test` | canonical top-level | A (hot) |
+| push | `push` | canonical top-level | A (hot) |
+| ready | `issue ready` | **yes** (existing) | A (hot) |
+| show | `issue show` | **yes** (existing) | A (hot) |
+| claim | `issue claim` | **yes** (existing) | A (hot) |
+| close | `issue close` | **yes** (existing) | A (hot) |
+| create | `issue create` | yes (existing, hidden) | B-alias |
+| update | `issue update` | yes (existing, hidden) | B-alias |
+| comment | `issue comment` | yes (hidden) | B-alias |
+| list | `issue list` | yes (existing, hidden) | B-alias |
+| blocked/stale/orphans/lint/claims/issues | `issue <sub>` | yes (existing, hidden) | B-alias |
+| stage | `issue stage` | yes (hidden) | B-alias |
+| recap | `issue recap` | yes (hidden) | B-alias |
+| export | `issue export` | yes (hidden) | B-alias |
+| sync | `issue sync` | **yes** (hot) | A/alias |
+| release | `issue release` (claim) | yes | B-alias |
+| release check | `pr release-check` *(or stays `release check`)* | — | **open Q** |
+| remember | `memory save` | **yes** (`remember`) | A (hot) |
+| recall | `memory recall` | **yes** (`recall`) | A (hot) |
+| insights | `memory insights` | optional | B-alias |
+| orient | `orient` | canonical top-level | A (hot) |
+| prime | `prime` | canonical top-level | A (hot) |
+| board | `team board` | optional | B-alias |
+| clean | `worktree clean` | **yes** (hot) | A/alias |
+| preflight | `pr preflight` | yes | B-alias |
+| shepherd | `pr shepherd` | yes | B-alias |
+| merge | `pr merge` | yes | B-alias |
+| doc-gate | `gate doc` | yes | B-alias |
+| init | `config init` | yes | B-alias |
+| setup | `config setup` | yes | B-alias |
+| options | `config options` | optional | B-alias |
+| role | `config role` | yes | B-alias |
+| recommend | `config recommend` | optional | B-alias |
+| explain | `config explain` | optional | B-alias |
+| hooks | `config hooks` | yes | B-alias |
+| new | `ext new` | yes | B-alias |
+| add | `ext add` | yes | B-alias |
+| adapter | `ext adapter` | canonical (exists) | B |
+| audit | `ext audit` | yes | B-alias |
