+| doctor | `env doctor` | yes | B-alias |
+| upgrade | `env upgrade` | yes | B-alias |
+| migrate | `env migrate` | yes | B-alias |
+
+**Result:** `forge --help` collapses from ~40 visible verbs to **9 base nouns +
+~15 hot shortcuts** — a learnable surface. Every one of the 57 verbs keeps working.
+
+---
+
+## 4. Resolving the crux — hot-path ergonomics
+
+Hard rule: heavily-used single-word verbs (`ready, show, status, claim, push,
+plan, dev, ship, test, remember, recall`) must NOT gain a keystroke.
+
+Resolution — three roles per verb (git/docker precedent):
+1. **Stays canonical top-level (no noun):** stages (`plan/dev/validate/ship/review/
+   verify`) and self-scoped hot reads (`status/orient/prime/push/test`). Stages are
+   bound 1:1 to `/plan`…`/verify` skills (AGENTS.md) — nesting them would break the
+   skill/stage model. These have *no* noun form.
+2. **Canonical is noun+sub, WITH a curated top-level alias:** `ready→issue ready`,
+   `show→issue show`, `claim`, `close`, `remember→memory save`, `recall→memory
+   recall`, `sync`, `clean`. Docs teach the noun; the bare verb keeps working and
+   stays visible in a "shortcuts" help footer.
+3. **Canonical is noun+sub, alias hidden (back-compat only):** the long tail
+   (`create/update/comment/preflight/merge/doctor/init/...`). Works forever, absent
+   from primary help — exactly today's `ISSUE_ALIAS_COMMANDS` treatment.
+
+The allowlist of *visible* hot verbs is a small curated constant (a superset of
+`ISSUE_ALIAS_COMMANDS`), reviewed deliberately — not every verb graduates to a
+visible shortcut.
+
+---
+
+## 5. Backward-compatibility & deprecation strategy
+
+Nothing breaks. Scripts, docs, AGENTS.md, CI, `.claude/commands/*` all keep working.
+
+1. **Generalise the alias mechanism.** Replace the single `ISSUE_ALIAS_COMMANDS`
+   list with a declarative map in one place, e.g.
+   `lib/commands/_aliases.js`: `{ alias → { canonical: 'memory save', visible: bool,
+   deprecated: bool } }`. The router already routes flat names; grouping is a
+   help/rendering layer + a dispatch table on the noun handlers.
+2. **Noun handlers dispatch to existing files.** `memory.js` etc. are thin
+   dispatchers (like `issue.js` → `_issue.js`) that route `save→remember.js`,
+   `recall→recall.js`. No handler logic moves initially — lowest-risk.
+3. **Deprecation is opt-in and quiet.** Aliases do NOT warn by default (avoids
+   breaking scripted stdout). A `FORGE_DEPRECATION_WARNINGS=1` env (or
+   `forge config options`) prints a one-line stderr hint: `forge doctor →
+   forge env doctor`. Never on stdout, never blocking. No removal is planned —
+   Docker still ships `docker pull` years later.
+4. **Help output** groups by noun (Tier B) + a "Shortcuts" footer (visible Tier A)
+   + hides the long-tail aliases — extends the existing `hidden`/`ISSUE_ALIAS`
+   filtering in `bin/forge.js:2608`.
+5. **Docs update approach:** AGENTS.md "Forge Issue Tracker" + push-workflow blocks
+   updated to teach noun forms with the shortcut noted inline
+   (`forge memory save <note>   # alias: forge remember`). A drift-checked command
+   manifest (`scripts/gen-command-manifest.js`) gains an alias-map assertion so the
+   help surface can't silently regress. `.claude/commands/*` slash commands (stages)
+   are unaffected (stages stay top-level).
+
+---
+
+## 6. Phased plan (lowest-risk / highest-clarity first)
+
+- **Phase 0 — Alias infrastructure (enabler).** Extract `_aliases.js` declarative
+  map + noun-grouped help renderer + optional stderr deprecation hint. No user-visible
+  rename yet. Unblocks every later phase; pure refactor of existing mechanism.
+- **Phase 1 — `memory`** (remember/recall/insights). Smallest, highest clarity, it's
+  the owner's named reference pattern. Proves the template end-to-end.
+- **Phase 2 — `config`** (init/setup/options/role/recommend/explain/hooks). High
+  clarity, low hot-path pressure (setup verbs are infrequent).
+- **Phase 3 — `ext`** (new/add/adapter/audit/patch). Extension authoring; niche users,
+  safe to regroup.
+- **Phase 4 — `env`** (doctor/upgrade/migrate) + fold `export`/`sync` into `issue`.
+- **Phase 5 — `pr`** (ship/preflight/shepherd/merge) + `gate doc`. Touches hot verbs
+  (`ship`) — do after the pattern is proven; `ship` keeps its top-level alias.
+- **Phase 6 — `issue` completion + help regroup.** Fold `comment/stage/recap`; ship
+  the final noun-grouped `forge --help`; land the manifest drift assertion.
+- **Phase 7 — Docs/AGENTS.md sweep.** Teach noun forms + shortcuts across AGENTS.md,
+  docs/reference/*, README; verify slash-command stages unaffected.
+
+Each phase is independently shippable and leaves the CLI fully working.
+
+---
+
+## 7. Open questions for the owner
+
+1. **`release` overload.** `release <id>` (release a claim) vs `release check`
+   (readiness gates) are two concepts. Split to `issue release` + `pr release-check`,
+   or keep `release check` as-is? Recommend split.
+2. **Base-noun names.** Are `env` and `ext` the right short nouns? Alternatives:
+   `env`→`sys`/`maint`; `ext`→`plugin`. Owner's rule is SHORT + easy to say — `env`/`ext`
+   are 3 letters but slightly technical.
+3. **`pr` vs `ship` as the base.** Group PR ops under `pr` (matches `gh pr`), or keep
+   `ship` the hero verb and nest the rest elsewhere? Recommend `pr` base + `ship` alias.
+4. **Visible-shortcut allowlist.** Confirm the ~15 verbs that stay visible top-level
+   (stages + status/push/test/ready/show/claim/close/remember/recall/orient/prime).
+   Which, if any, should be demoted to hidden?
+5. **Deprecation hints.** OK to ship stderr hints behind `FORGE_DEPRECATION_WARNINGS=1`
+   (default off, never removed), or keep aliases entirely silent forever?
